# Spider-Man No More {1}{U}: "Enchant creature. Enchanted creature is a Citizen with base power and toughness 1/1. It has defender and loses
# all other abilities." Black Lotus pays on turn 3 (Bot1 enchants Bot2's Ornithopter, a colorless 0/2 Thopter artifact creature with flying).
# "Is a Citizen" replaces its creature types only (CR 205.1a): it stays an artifact creature and colorless. It is 1/1 (CR 613.4b), and its
# flying is lost while the defender granted after the loss is kept (CR 613.1f, 613.7), so on turn 4 it cannot attack (CR 702.3b) while Bot2's Memnite can: Bot1 takes 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Spider-Man No More
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Memnite
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Spider-Man No More.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Spider-Man No More.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Subtypes = Citizen
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Types = Artifact; Creature
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Colors = (absent)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Defender
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
Bot2.Attack(Memnite > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Spider-Man No More.Subtypes = Aura
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Defender
Bot1.Life = 19
